			"Message": "docs(Project): Remove Grove references from Vine architecture documentation\n\nThe Grove WASM extension host component was removed from the active protocol layer. This update removes dead references to `Grove.proto`, the Grove gRPC client, and the `NetworkGrovePort` configuration from the Vine architecture documentation across `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md`, `Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md`, and the root `README.md`.\n\nThe gRPC topology is now streamlined to Mountain ↔ Cocoon (Vine/Spine prototypes) and Mountain ↔ Air (Air.proto). The documentation diagrams, tables, and port listings are updated to reflect the current production stack.",
			"SHA": "f7e1043f334b29028a153f2e1570b7d908e3fa88"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T18:40:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				111,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Add blank lines after match arms and inline declarations in generated code and notification handlers\n\nIntroduce consistent blank line separators after match arm bodies and variable declarations across DevLog, Error, and the generated Vine protobuf runtime. This improves readability in conditional blocks and struct definitions without altering logic.\n\nUpdate notification handlers (OutputChannelCoalesce, RegisterCommand, SetTextEditorDecorations, UpdateScmGroup, WebviewLifecycle) to add blank lines before key operations like buffer pushes, batch collections, and match arm outcomes. These formatting adjustments align with Rust style conventions for separating logical statement groups.\n\nThe changes are cosmetic only, enhancing code clarity in the gRPC protocol definitions and their server-side handling.",
			"SHA": "90b7bd7365a3942857211657fe266fa2f6050eed"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:23:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				111,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Consolidate multiplexer notification publisher\n\nRemove the `PublishNotificationFromMux` public module export and update the multiplexer read pump to call `PublishNotification::Fn` directly. The publisher logic remains in `PublishNotification` (now the sole entry point) while the wrapper module is eliminated.\n\nThis reduces the client module surface by removing a trivial re-export layer, aligning with the consolidation pattern seen in recent notification and provider unregistration refactors.",
			"SHA": "c48ca0fa2432d44963553427391398249b3b127a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:22:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				110,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Consolidate notification mod.rs to retain only non-trivial handlers\n\nRemove pure-relay notification modules that perform single-step delegation (OutputAppend, OutputChannelClear/Create/Dispose/Replace/Show, OutputClear/Create/Dispose, ProgressComplete/Update, WindowShowTextDocument, WorkspaceApplyEdit, ExtensionActivated/Deactivated, TreeRefresh, ExtensionHostMessage, LanguagesSetDocumentLanguage, WebviewReady) which are now inlined directly in Mountain's dispatcher.\n\nUpdate module documentation to clarify the retention criteria: handlers must have payload reshaping, channel-drain coalescing, multiple side effects, or non-obvious Sky-event mapping. Retain OutputChannelCoalesce and ProgressStart/End/Report as they implement channel-drain coalescers.\n\nThis reduction from ~45 to ~20 modules streamlines the notification surface while preserving all handlers with genuine orchestration complexity.",
			"SHA": "74f76952aeba7c2b4f442c7ce9d1a54d169bfb66"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:08:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				110,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Inline trivial provider unregistration atoms\n\nRemove the wrapper modules `UnregisterFileSystemProvider` and `UnregisterUriHandler` from the notification tree. These atoms performed only single-step delegation to `UnregisterByHandle` with scheme logging, which is now handled directly in Mountain's dispatcher.\n\nRetain `UnregisterScmProvider` as it contains the DJB-31 handle recomputation logic, `UnregisterProvider` call, Sky event relay, and detailed logging.\n\nThis consolidates the unregistration surface to only expose atoms with genuine multi-step orchestration needs.",
			"SHA": "a254bd2d8976d0b8d403199a9ee908b7eddaa60f"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1780506230545
}